sequenceDiagram
    actor Client
    participant PostResource
    participant PostService
    participant Post
    participant Author
    participant JPA
    participant PostgreSQL

    Client->>PostResource: POST posts with Post body
    activate PostResource
    
    PostResource->>Post: new Post
    activate Post
    deactivate Post
    
    Note over Post: Client instantiates Post with constructor parameters
    
    PostResource->>Post: setTitle(title), setContent(content), setAuthor(author)
    activate Post
    deactivate Post
    
    Note over Post: Post object fields are populated
    
    Post->>Author: reference established
    activate Author
    deactivate Author
    
    Note over Post,Author: Author reference is established via ManyToOne relationship
    
    PostResource->>PostService: insert(post)
    activate PostService
    
    Note over PostResource,PostService: post: populated Post object
    
    PostService->>JPA: persist(post)
    activate JPA
    
    Note over PostService,JPA: JPA persists Post entity to PostgreSQL database
    
    JPA->>PostgreSQL: INSERT INTO post (title, content, author_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?)
    activate PostgreSQL
    
    PostgreSQL-->>JPA: return generated ID
    deactivate PostgreSQL
    
    Note over PostgreSQL,JPA: Autogenerated primary key via IDENTITY strategy
    
    JPA->>Post: setId(generatedId)
    activate Post
    deactivate Post
    
    Note over JPA,Post: Database generates ID via IDENTITY strategy
    
    deactivate JPA
    
    PostService-->>PostResource: return post
    deactivate PostService
    
    Note over PostService,PostResource: Managed Post entity with generated ID
    
    PostResource-->>Client: ResponseEntity.created(uri).body(post)
    deactivate PostResource
    
    Note over PostResource,Client: HTTP 201 Created with Location header and Post is returned to client